2026-11-27T10:19:40.0502621Z -- v5.3.0 — defrost: duty is measured, the derate is physics
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0502904Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0503056Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0503201Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0503316Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0503540Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0503685Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0503857Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0504037Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0504146Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0504271Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0504432Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0504601Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0504745Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0504929Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0505058Z   ok   an untouched bucket still derates nothing
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0505322Z   ok   the summary says which estimator a bucket rests on, and how many defrosts were actually witnessed
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0505478Z   ok   a duty outside [0, 1] is refused, not folded into the bucket
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0505699Z   ok   the range guard rejects only OUTSIDE [0, 1] — 0 and 1 still fold
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0505876Z   ok   a pre-v5.3.0 store loads without raising, and says it was upgraded
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0506002Z   ok   its learned factors are KEPT, not discarded
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0506160Z   ok   but the estimator's optimistic tail is clamped away on load
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0506324Z   ok   a measured duty then overrides the carried-over inference
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0506479Z   ok   a v2 store round-trips exactly
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0506654Z   ok   a v2 store still carries factors/counts, so a DOWNGRADE loads too
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0506804Z   ok   a garbage store loads as empty rather than raising (None)
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0507128Z   ok   a garbage store loads as empty rather than raising ({})
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0507275Z   ok   a garbage store loads as empty rather than raising ([])
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0507491Z   ok   a garbage store loads as empty rather than raising ('nope')
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0507710Z   ok   a garbage store loads as empty rather than raising ({'factors': 'bad', 'duty': 3})
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0507904Z   ok   a window whose clock cannot be compared measures nothing, and is refused
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0508145Z   ok   inside 0-5 °C an interval with NO defrost now teaches the COP scale
2026-11-27T10:19:40.0508302Z   ok   and an interval that DID contain a defrost is still refused
